>OK, Here's an opinion question...  I have a scroll of blank paper
>and a magic marker (66).  
>
>if I understand it correctly, I can "apply" the magic marker to
>the blank scroll and write my own scroll.  The question is
>
>What to write?
>

Don't write anything yet.

Before you write, find an altar and drop the scroll and the marker
on it to find out their blessed/cursed status.  (to avoid a nasty 
surprise it you try to genocide cockatrices with a cursed scroll).

Secondly, you have a clear potion (water).  Once you find an altar
you may want to drop the water on it to make it holy/unholy.  Then
you can dip your magic marker in it to get a blessed/cursed one.

The relationship between scroll, marker, and the resultant scroll
goes like this:

                blessed marker   uncursed marker  cursed marker

blessed scroll     blessed           blessed        uncursed
uncursed scroll    blessed           uncursed       cursed
cursed scroll      uncursed          cursed         cursed

Once you've figured all that out, remember that a tourist has only
a very slim chance of writing a scroll he/she hasn't already seen.
I'd only try to write a scroll you've already seen.  Here are the
ones I might write if you've seen them/depending on the circumstances
when you get to that stage.

Charging (blessed only): for the magic marker, if you have other blank scrolls
Enchant armor: if you have somehting like speed boots you want to rustproof
               Possibly also use a blessed one to enchant the armor, but don't
               waste it on your current armor.
Enchant weapon: if you have a good weapon you want to rustproof
               Possible also use a blessed one to enchant a weapon, but don't
               waste it on your darts.
Genocide (Cursed or blessed): Be careful with the cursed one.
Identify: Only if you have several things your really need to identify
Remove curse: Only if you really need it
Scare monster: Could be a life saver early on
Taming: Again, could save your life
Teleportation: A cursed one could be really helpful

